#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:13
msgid "Migrations"
msgstr "Migreringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:15
msgid ""
"Migrations are a means of facilitating database changes, much in the same "
"way UMIL was used in phpBB 3.0. Through Migrations, extension developers are"
" able to easily modify and add new schema and data to the database as "
"required by an extension."
msgstr ""
"Migreringer er en måde at facilitere databaseændringer på, meget på samme "
"måde som UMIL blev brugt i phpBB 3.0. Gennem migreringer kan "
"udvidelsesudviklere nemt ændre og tilføje nyt skema og data til databasen, "
"som en udvidelse kræver det."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:20
msgid ""
"Read the Migrations: :doc:`../migrations/getting_started` Developer Docs for"
" in-depth migration documentation. We will briefly summarise the key "
"concepts of migrations here."
msgstr ""
"Læs udviklerdokumentationen Migrations: :doc:`../migrations/getting_started`"
" for uddybende migreringsdokumentation. Vi vil kort opsummere de vigtigste "
"koncepter for migreringer her."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:26
msgid ""
"The phpBB Customisation Database `Migrations Validation Policy "
"<https://www.phpbb.com/extensions/rules-and-policies/validation-"
"policy/#migrations>`_."
msgstr ""
"phpBB's `valideringspolitik for migreringer "
"<https://www.phpbb.com/extensions/rules-and-policies/validation-"
"policy/#migrations>`_ i Customisation Database."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:29
msgid "Database changes"
msgstr "Databaseændringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:32
msgid "Schema changes"
msgstr "Skemaændringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:34
msgid ""
"The ``update_schema()`` method is for facilitating schema changes, such as "
"adding new tables, columns, keys and indexes."
msgstr ""
"``update_schema()``-metoden er til at facilitere skemaændringer, såsom "
"tilføjelse af nye tabeller, kolonner, nøgler og indekser."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:37
msgid ""
"The ``revert_schema()`` method should always be including to undo any "
"changes introduced by the ``update_schema()`` method."
msgstr ""
"``revert_schema()``-metoden bør altid inkluderes for at fortryde eventuelle "
"ændringer introduceret af ``update_schema()``-metoden."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:40
msgid "We recommend putting schema changes in their own migration."
msgstr "Vi anbefaler at placere skemaændringer i deres egen migrering."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:42
msgid "Learn more: :doc:`../migrations/schema_changes`."
msgstr "Læs mere: :doc:`../migrations/schema_changes`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:45
msgid "Data changes"
msgstr "Dataændringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:47
msgid ""
"The ``update_data()`` method is for inserting, updating and dropping field "
"data."
msgstr ""
"``update_data()``-metoden er til at indsætte, opdatere og fjerne feltdata."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:50
msgid ""
"The ``revert_data()`` method is optional and can be used to undo data "
"changes. Normally, the ``update_data()`` method is automatically reverted "
"during a purge step, reversing any of the changes introduced by the "
"migration tools. Using the ``revert_data()`` method is only needed to "
"perform additional changes during an extension's uninstall, such as "
"performing a custom functions."
msgstr ""
"``revert_data()``-metoden er valgfri og kan bruges til at fortryde "
"dataændringer. Normalt fortrydes ``update_data()``-metoden automatisk under "
"et purge-trin, hvilket omgør enhver ændring introduceret af "
"migreringsværktøjerne. Brug af ``revert_data()``-metoden er kun nødvendig "
"for at udføre yderligere ændringer under afinstallation af en udvidelse, "
"såsom at udføre en brugerdefineret funktion."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:57
msgid "We recommend putting data changes in their own migration."
msgstr "Vi anbefaler at placere dataændringer i deres egen migrering."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:59
msgid "Learn more: :doc:`../migrations/data_changes`."
msgstr "Læs mere: :doc:`../migrations/data_changes`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:62
msgid "Migration tools"
msgstr "Migreringsværktøjer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:64
msgid ":doc:`../migrations/tools/config`"
msgstr ":doc:`../migrations/tools/config`"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:65
msgid "The config tool helps adding, updating, and removing config items."
msgstr ""
"Config-værktøjet hjælper med at tilføje, opdatere og fjerne config-"
"elementer."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:67
msgid ":doc:`../migrations/tools/config_text`"
msgstr ":doc:`../migrations/tools/config_text`"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:68
msgid ""
"The config_text tool helps adding, updating, and removing config_text items."
" The config_text table is used to store options with an arbitrary length "
"value in a TEXT column. In contrast to config values, config_text are not "
"cached or prefetched."
msgstr ""
"config_text-værktøjet hjælper med at tilføje, opdatere og fjerne "
"config_text-elementer. Tabellen config_text bruges til at gemme "
"indstillinger med en vilkårligt lang værdi i en TEXT-kolonne. I modsætning "
"til config-værdier bliver config_text hverken cachet eller forudhentet."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:73
msgid ":doc:`../migrations/tools/module`"
msgstr ":doc:`../migrations/tools/module`"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:74
msgid "The module tool helps adding and removing ACP, MCP, and UCP modules."
msgstr ""
"Modulværktøjet hjælper med at tilføje og fjerne ACP-, MCP- og UCP-moduler."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:76
msgid ":doc:`../migrations/tools/permission`"
msgstr ":doc:`../migrations/tools/permission`"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:77
msgid ""
"The permission tool helps adding, removing, setting, and unsetting "
"permissions and adding or removing permission roles."
msgstr ""
"Tilladelsesværktøjet hjælper med at tilføje, fjerne, aktivere og deaktivere "
"tilladelser samt tilføje eller fjerne tilladelsesroller."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:81
msgid "Migration dependencies"
msgstr "Migreringsafhængigheder"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:84
msgid "depends_on()"
msgstr "depends_on()"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:86
msgid ""
"The ``depends_on()`` method is used to define a migration's dependencies. "
"Dependencies tell the migrator what order migrations must be installed in."
msgstr ""
"``depends_on()``-metoden bruges til at definere en migrerings afhængigheder."
" Afhængigheder fortæller migratoren, i hvilken rækkefølge migreringer skal "
"installeres."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:89
msgid "Learn more: :doc:`../migrations/dependencies`."
msgstr "Læs mere: :doc:`../migrations/dependencies`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:92
msgid "effectively_installed()"
msgstr "effectively_installed()"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:94
msgid ""
"The ``effectively_installed()`` method is used primarily to help transition "
"from a previous database installer method (such as a MOD that used UMIL) to "
"migrations. However, we recommend using it all the time to ensure safer "
"migrations."
msgstr ""
"``effectively_installed()``-metoden bruges primært til at hjælpe med "
"overgangen fra en tidligere databaseinstallationsmetode (såsom en MOD, der "
"brugte UMIL) til migreringer. Vi anbefaler dog at bruge den hele tiden for "
"at sikre sikrere migreringer."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:99
msgid ""
"When effectively_installed returns true, the migration is deemed to already "
"have been installed, meaning the migration will be skipped. This helps "
"prevent rewriting (or overwriting) existing changes to the database that may"
" have already been put in place by a previous migration or MOD installation."
msgstr ""
"Når effectively_installed returnerer true, anses migreringen for allerede at"
" være installeret, hvilket betyder, at migreringen springes over. Dette "
"hjælper med at forhindre omskrivning (eller overskrivning) af eksisterende "
"ændringer i databasen, som allerede kan være blevet foretaget af en "
"tidligere migrering eller MOD-installation."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:105
msgid ""
"For example, in the following code the migration would not be applied if the"
" specified config value already exists in the database:"
msgstr ""
"I følgende kode ville migreringen f.eks. ikke blive anvendt, hvis den "
"angivne config-værdi allerede findes i databasen:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:117
msgid ""
"As a general rule, migrations should never be changed once they have been "
"installed. Changing a migration in an extension that has already been "
"installed could prevent it from reverting database changes or uninstalling "
"successfully. In order to make subsequent changes to the database, new "
"migrations should be created to implement the additional changes or updates."
" The only exceptions to this rule are to fix SQL and logic errors or bugs, "
"as long as they do not alter the database changes that have already been "
"made or the dependencies listed in the migration's ``depends_on()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Som en generel regel bør migreringer aldrig ændres, når de er blevet "
"installeret. At ændre en migrering i en udvidelse, der allerede er "
"installeret, kunne forhindre den i at fortryde databaseændringer eller blive"
" afinstalleret korrekt. For at foretage efterfølgende ændringer i databasen "
"bør der oprettes nye migreringer til at implementere de yderligere ændringer"
" eller opdateringer. De eneste undtagelser til denne regel er at rette SQL- "
"og logikfejl eller bugs, så længe de ikke ændrer de databaseændringer, der "
"allerede er foretaget, eller de afhængigheder, der er angivet i migreringens"
" ``depends_on()``-metode."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_migrations.rst:126
msgid ""
"Once you are familiar with how Migrations work, continue on to the next "
"section to learn how to create and install an ACP module that will allow us "
"to configure some settings for the Acme Demo extension."
msgstr ""
"Når du er fortrolig med, hvordan migreringer fungerer, fortsæt til næste "
"afsnit for at lære, hvordan man opretter og installerer et ACP-modul, som "
"giver os mulighed for at konfigurere nogle indstillinger for Acme Demo-"
"udvidelsen."
